sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To circumscribe a circle about a given square.
----
proof:

Let {ABCD|square} be the given square.

It is required to circumscribe a circle about the square {ABCD|square}.

Join {AC} and {BD}, and let them cut one another at {E}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.9 diagram" src="propIV9.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The two diagonals, the I.8 bisection of the angles of the square, the
    // I.6 equality of the four half-diagonals, then the circle.
    //
    // Joyce's figure builds the square from its circle: A and C are free,
    // E their midpoint, B and D at right angles about E. The walk follows
    // the proof instead — the square given, the circle last — which the
    // figure supports unchanged: the circle ABCD is simply left out of the
    // visible sets until "Let it be circumscribed".
    //
    // Everything added leaves the resting figure as it was: the four sides
    // DA, AB, BC, DC and the four half-diagonals EA, EB, EC, ED are
    // transparent highlight targets (the figure draws them only as parts of
    // the square and of AC and BD), and the angle markers are hidden at rest.
    //
    // Angle markers: the angles of the square DAB, ABC, BCD, CDA are purple;
    // the halves DAC, BAC (= EAB) and EBA blue. The proof never calls the
    // angles of the square right, so they are sectors, not right-angle
    // marks. At A and B the halves lie side by side inside the whole angle,
    // so halves are pinned at 22 px and wholes at 34 px.
    var GIVEN = ["square","A","B","C","D","DA","AB","BC","DC"];
    var JOIN  = GIVEN.concat(["AC","BD","E","EA","EB","EC","ED"]);
    var BIS   = JOIN.concat(["angDAC","angBAC"]);
    var WHOLE = BIS.concat(["angDAB"]);
    var SIM   = WHOLE.concat(["angABC","angBCD","angCDA"]);
    var HALF  = SIM.concat(["angEBA"]);
    var CIRC  = JOIN.concat(["ABCD","ABCDc"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IV.9",
        pivot: "E",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;140,30",
            "C;point;free;140,235",
            "E;point;midpoint;A,C;black;green",
            "ABCD;circle;radius;E,A;0;0;black;random",
            "B;point;perpendicular;E,A",
            "D;point;perpendicular;E,C",
            "square;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;black;random",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            // The sides and half-diagonals the proof names (see above).
            "DA;line;connect;D,A;0;0;0",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C;0;0;0",
            "DC;line;connect;D,C;0;0;0",
            "EA;line;connect;E,A;0;0;0",
            "EB;line;connect;E,B;0;0;0",
            "EC;line;connect;E,C;0;0;0",
            "ED;line;connect;E,D;0;0;0",
            // A transparent twin of the circle carries its highlight and
            // hover: the circle's own face is opaque, and a highlighted
            // element is promoted within its draw pass (#140), so lighting
            // ABCD itself would paint over the square.
            "ABCDc;circle;radius;E,A;0;0;0;0",
            "angDAC;sector;angleMarker;A,D,C,22;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angBAC;sector;angleMarker;A,B,C,22;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angEBA;sector;angleMarker;B,E,A,22;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angDAB;sector;angleMarker;A,D,B,34;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angABC;sector;angleMarker;B,A,C,34;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angBCD;sector;angleMarker;C,B,D,34;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angCDA;sector;angleMarker;D,C,A,34;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6"
        ],
        // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A and C free, both
        // vertices of the given square, so they stand from slide 1 and are
        // not deferred. B and D (perpendicular) and E (midpoint) are derived
        // and listed per slide; E arrives with the diagonals.
        // The circle owns ABCD in prose; the square takes {ABCD|square}, and
        // the circle itself is lit through its twin, {ABCD|ABCDc}.
        aliases: { "BA": "AB", "AD": "DA", "CD": "DC", "CB": "BC",
                   "DB": "BD", "CA": "AC",
                   "AE": "EA", "BE": "EB", "CE": "EC", "DE": "ED",
                   "DAC": "angDAC", "CAD": "angDAC",
                   "BAC": "angBAC", "CAB": "angBAC",
                   "EAB": "angBAC", "BAE": "angBAC",
                   "EBA": "angEBA", "ABE": "angEBA",
                   "DAB": "angDAB", "BAD": "angDAB",
                   "ABC": "angABC", "CBA": "angABC",
                   "BCD": "angBCD", "DCB": "angBCD",
                   "CDA": "angCDA", "ADC": "angCDA" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To circumscribe a circle about a given square.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["square"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "IV.9" }] },
            { text: "Let {ABCD|square} be the given square.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["square"] },
            { text: "It is required to circumscribe a circle about the square {ABCD|square}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["square"] },
            { text: "Join {AC} and {BD}, and let them cut one another at {E}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AC","BD","E"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "BD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "E",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Then, since {DA} equals {AB}, and {AC} is common,",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["DA","AB","AC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "the sides of a square are equal", ref: "I.Def.22" }] },
            { text: "therefore the two sides {DA} and {AC} equal the two sides {BA} and {AC},",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["DA","AB","AC"] },
            { text: "and the base {DC} equals the base {BC},",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["DC","BC"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {DAC} equals the angle {BAC}.",
              visible: BIS,
              highlighted: ["angDAC","angBAC"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angDAC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angBAC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle DAC = angle BAC", ref: "I.8" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the angle {DAB} is bisected by {AC}.",
              visible: WHOLE,
              highlighted: ["angDAB","AC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angDAB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that each of the angles {ABC}, {BCD}, and {CDA} is bisected by the straight lines {AC} and {DB}.",
              visible: SIM,
              highlighted: ["angABC","angBCD","angCDA","AC","BD"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angABC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angBCD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angCDA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Now, since the angle {DAB} equals the angle {ABC},",
              visible: SIM,
              highlighted: ["angDAB","angABC"] },
            { text: "and the angle {EAB} is half of the angle {DAB}, and the angle {EBA} half of the angle {ABC},",
              visible: HALF,
              highlighted: ["angBAC","angDAB","angEBA","angABC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angEBA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the angle {EAB} also equals the angle {EBA},",
              visible: HALF,
              highlighted: ["angBAC","angEBA"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "halves of equal angles", ref: "C.N.5" }] },
            { text: "so that the side {EA} also equals {EB}.",
              visible: HALF,
              highlighted: ["EA","EB","angBAC","angEBA"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "sides opposite equal angles are equal", ref: "I.6" }] },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that each of the straight lines {EA} and {EB} equals each of the straight lines {EC} and {ED}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["EA","EB","EC","ED"] },
            { text: "Therefore the four straight lines {EA}, {EB}, {EC}, and {ED} equal one another.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["EA","EB","EC","ED"] },
            { text: "Therefore the circle described with center {E} and radius one of the straight lines {EA}, {EB}, {EC}, or {ED}",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["E","EA","EB","EC","ED"] },
            { text: "also passes through the remaining points, and it is circumscribed about the square {ABCD|square}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["A","B","C","D","square"] },
            { text: "Let it be circumscribed, as {ABCD|ABCDc}.",
              visible: CIRC,
              highlighted: ["ABCDc"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "ABCD", name: geomlib.A.Circle.compass } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.3" }] },
            { text: "Therefore a circle has been circumscribed about the given square.",
              visible: CIRC,
              highlighted: ["ABCDc","square"],
              justifications: [
                  { claim: "the circle passes through each angle of the square", ref: "IV.Def.6" },
                  { ref: "Q.E.F." } ] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "IV.9") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Def.22": "/elements/books/bookI/definitions/defI22/",
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.Post.3": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post3/",
        "C.N.5":    "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn5/",
        "I.6":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI6/",
        "I.8":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI8/",
        "IV.Def.6": "/elements/books/bookIV/definitions/defIV6/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Then, since {DA} equals {AB}, and {AC} is common, therefore the two sides {DA} and {AC} equal the two sides {BA} and {AC}, and the base {DC} equals the base {BC}, therefore the angle {DAC} equals the angle {BAC}. [!just I.8]

Therefore the angle {DAB} is bisected by {AC}.

Similarly we can prove that each of the angles {ABC}, {BCD}, and {CDA} is bisected by the straight lines {AC} and {DB}.

Now, since the angle {DAB} equals the angle {ABC}, and the angle {EAB} is half of the angle {DAB}, and the angle {EBA} half of the angle {ABC}, therefore the angle {EAB} also equals the angle {EBA}, so that the side {EA} also equals {EB}. [!just I.6]

Similarly we can prove that each of the straight lines {EA} and {EB} equals each of the straight lines {EC} and {ED}.

Therefore the four straight lines {EA}, {EB}, {EC}, and {ED} equal one another.

Therefore the circle described with center {E} and radius one of the straight lines {EA}, {EB}, {EC}, or {ED} also passes through the remaining points, and it is circumscribed about the square {ABCD|square}.

Let it be circumscribed, as {ABCD|ABCDc}.

Therefore a circle has been circumscribed about the given square.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
----
guide: This is a straightforward proposition, one of four in the sequence @IV.6 through IV.9 about circles and squares.
